{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 78.7% similarity to plant defensin Vv-AMP1. GRAVY: -0.91; Mol Wt: 5466.339; Mol formula: C220H358N86O61S8. Most positively charged plant defensin identified today (also in the APD as of May 2019). Chemical modification: The 4 disulfide bonds were included as restraints in the structure calculations: Cys3-Cys47; Cys14-Cys34; Cys20-Cys41; and Cys24-Cys43. Structure: it contains 3 beta strands and one helix. Two prolines in trans conformation. Activity: Recombinant peptide is active against bacteria S. aureus ATCC 9144 (IC50 1.5 uM), B. subtilis (IC50 0.4 uM), and P. aeruginosa PAO1 (IC50 1.7 uM). Fungi: Also active against C. albicans in both the yeast and biofilm form as well as other Candida species, the filamentous fungus F. graminearum and E. coli in media containing 100 mM NaCl (salt-insensitive). Other fungi inhibited are C. auris (IC50 3.4 uM), C. glabrata ATCC 90030 (IC50 1.2 uM), C. krusei (IC50 0.9 uM), C. parapsilosis (IC50 1.3 uM), C. tropicalis ATCC 750 (IC50 0.5 uM), F. graminearum PH-1 (IC50 1.0 uM). Antimicrobial robustness: NaCl-insensitive:C. albicans (100 mM); NaCl-insensitive:C. krusei (100 mM); MgCl2-insensitive:C. albicans (5 mM); CaCl2-insensitive:C. albicans (2 mM); Recombinant production:bacteria:Escherichia coli: established. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31031739", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2019 Apr 12;10:795. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2019.00795. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03072", "source_id": "AP03072", "source_numeric_id": "03072", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03072", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Salt-Tolerant Antifungal and Antibacterial Activities of the Corn Defensin ZmD32", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
